prompt:
You are responding in a synthetic research interview as the assigned traveller. Do not act as an adviser or invent market facts. Your profile does not prescribe a purchase choice. Evaluate the offer as described, not as a better imagined product.
{"brief": "An AI travel assistant that helps people plan and navigate trips.", "offer": "Build and edit an itinerary, combine travellers' preferences, organise booking details and suggest changes during the trip. Users verify recommendations and approve bookings. No autonomous purchases or human concierge are included.", "question": "Who would consider paying, for which benefit, and why choose this over ChatGPT or free travel tools?", "evidence": [{"id": "TR01", "title": "Mindtrip traveller FAQs", "url": "https://resources.mindtrip.ai/travelers/help/traveler-faqs", "observation": "Vendor describes conversational recommendations, editable itineraries, collaboration, booking organisation and in-trip maps.", "limit": "Feature baseline only. Does not establish independent performance or payment demand.", "checked": "2026-09-20"}, {"id": "TR02", "title": "Layla", "url": "https://layla.ai/", "observation": "Vendor advertises AI trip planning and optional human travel experts.", "limit": "No verified price benchmark. Human support is outside this study's offer.", "checked": "2026-09-20"}, {"id": "TR03", "title": "Booking.com AI sentiment report", "url": "https://news.booking.com/bookingcom-releases-the-global-ai-sentiment-report/", "observation": "2025 survey of 37,325 people in 33 markets reports interest in AI travel planning and limited comfort with autonomous AI decisions.", "limit": "Industry-sponsored self-report. Does not establish paid conversion or audience proportions.", "checked": "2026-09-20"}]}
No price has been set. consider_paying means conditional interest, not a purchase or conversion. Return only JSON with decision (consider_paying, free_only or decline), reason, valuable_feature, objection, next_test, and scenario {hours_saved_per_trip, value_per_hour_gbp, trips_per_year, rationale}. The scenario numbers are your explicit hypothetical assumptions, not measured facts or willingness to pay. Use zero if no time saving. next_test must describe a concrete real-world experiment, not a source ID. Check that numerical assumptions are internally consistent with their rationale. Keep every string under 55 words.
